{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01P6gbPGHUG1fe6ANmRvVrwt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-folder, local-first personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown into a trio-driven R&D \"mission control.\" Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a personal task/project manager backed by plain markdown.** The source of truth is markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) â€” no database, no lock files. Tasks move through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved â†’ Restored).\n\n- **It ships two interfaces over the same logic.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary app â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the full dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes directly to the markdown files. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror that shares the same format/paths and also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It runs persistently as a Windows service.** The `anchor` NSSM service (auto-start, LocalSystem) owns the process and binds `127.0.0.1:8777`; you don't launch it by hand. A daily 5 AM `anchor_healthcheck.py` self-test (Task Scheduler) parses every file, exercises every endpoint, and writes `health_reports/`.\n\n- **It layers an R&D control surface (v2 + v3) on top.** Each project becomes a row that can launch the \"trio\" â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build) â€” and remembers that work as **sessions** with cached, validated, grounded summaries (goal Â· decisions Â· doc links Â· effort).\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\" adds real terminals and isolation.** ConPTY terminal sessions (the one declared native-dep exception, optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking draggable window manager, in-place expandable session summaries, stage handoffs (plan-set â†’ build), a runnable deliverable preview guarded never to bind 8777, and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Its declared deliverable is `anchor_gui.py` itself** â€” the running dashboard server is pinned as the Anchor deliverable and can be spun up as an ephemeral, isolated preview.\n\n- **Hard constraints it enforces:** Python 3.8+ stdlib only (single `pywinpty` exception, lazy, terminal-only, in `pty_manager.py`), one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, no OneDrive/syncing), all files human-readable/CLI-accessible, no binary or compiled assets.\n\nStatus per memory: v2 is built and merged to master (2026-06-11); v3 is built by Foreman (all 10 waves green, 529 tests) but **not yet merged/deployed** as of today."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20212,"cache_read_input_tokens":20573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20212},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90c1417f-86eb-432b-9ec4-72d40cd66384","uuid":"93f96460-b5d0-4a6f-8854-adb66fae5122","request_id":"req_011CbyGtJNPt6KMeW1ZqmokN"}
